.TH KAGI-SECURITY-CHECK 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "Developer Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-security-check \- run Kagi's local security and robustness checks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash scripts/kagi-security-check
.RB [ quick | deep ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The default
.B quick
mode checks formatting for the Rust and fuzz workspaces and compiles, tests,
and runs Clippy with warnings denied for the default, QUIC, and userspace
eBPF builds.
.TP
.B deep
Run the quick checks, then scan Rust dependencies, record unsafe-code
inventory, run Miri and the address and thread sanitizers, and run the
repository's fuzz smoke tests.
The deep checks need a compatible nightly Rust toolchain and the tools
listed in the repository's security validation guide.
The unsafe-code inventory is written to
.IR target/kagi-security/geiger.txt .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KAGI_INSTALL_TOOLS
Set to 1 to let deep mode install missing Cargo subcommands and the nightly
toolchain.
Deep mode also ensures that nightly has the Miri and rust-src components.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coverage (1),
.BR test-all (1)
